      "This matters for two reasons. First, a rotted jamb is often sitting against a rotted buck, so the repair can be larger than it looks. Second, impact-rated entry doors are tested as a complete assembly, including the frame and the anchoring into the wall. The installation has to follow the door's Florida Product Approval or Miami-Dade NOA.",
      "## Rotted Door Jamb: What Causes It",
      "Rotted door jamb repair is one of the most common small exterior repairs in Florida, and the cause is almost always the same: water sitting at the bottom of the frame. Typical culprits:",
